# These tests intentionally call CoCreateInstance with COM uninitialized.
# On Brave's Windows ASan bots, that error path grows the CRT exit-handler
# table through _register_onexit_function -> _recalloc_base -> _msize_base.
# ASan's HeapSize interceptor rejects the existing buffer as not owned by ASan,
# aborting before the tests can check CO_E_NOTINITIALIZED. The COM test code is
# unmodified upstream code; COM hook patching is compiled out on x64.
# All 288 reports are Windows x64 ASan failures. Upstream LUCI Analysis shows
# 0% failures/flakes over 30 days (2026-11-05); each test has 530 passing Windows
# ASan runs, all on Windows-10-19045. Filter only Windows ASan for this failure.
# https://github.com/brave/brave-browser/issues/58155
# https://github.com/brave/brave-browser/issues/58156
# https://github.com/brave/brave-browser/issues/58157
# https://github.com/brave/brave-browser/issues/58158
-ComInitCheckHook.AssertNotInitialized
-ComInitCheckHook.HookRemoval
-ComInitCheckHook.MultipleHooks
-TestComInitBalancer.UnbalancedPairsWithComBalancerDisabled
